schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-mermaid-01-canonical-widget
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: kino-mermaid
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: canonical-widget
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook documentation engineer. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.Mermaid. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Use current core Kino.Mermaid behavior.
  text: |-
    Create a canonical Kino.Mermaid Livebook cell. Install core Kino, build a Mermaid flowchart or sequence diagram in an Elixir heredoc, and render it with Kino.Mermaid.new/1. Include a clear diagram type token on the first nonblank line, quoted labels for special characters, classDef styling, and a small data-driven variant that builds a sequence diagram from a list of safe tuples or maps.

    Requirements: document Livebook/Kino compatibility and that this is static SVG output, not a Jupyter ipywidgets control; describe the diagram source shape and supported diagram type; include accessible title/summary text near the diagram; include fallback comments for old Kino versions; and include safe execution checks for untrusted labels, Mermaid control characters, eval, shell calls, credentials, and remote libraries.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-mermaid-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino and renders Kino.Mermaid.new/1 as the primary output."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino runtime and static SVG behavior."
  - "Reactive state: generated diagram source is deterministic; dynamic changes require rerunning the cell or regenerating source."
  - "Data shape: Mermaid source string, first-line type token, quoted labels, and optional data-driven steps are documented."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: diagram has a readable title or summary and a fallback note for old Kino versions."
  - "Safe execution: untrusted labels are escaped or sanitized; no eval, shell commands, credentials, remote libraries, or unsafe control characters."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The Mermaid source starts with a valid diagram type token and uses real newlines."
    - "The code is valid Elixir and calls Kino.Mermaid.new/1."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Implements a canonical Mermaid diagram with styling and an optional data-driven source example."
    - "Uses Kino.Mermaid-specific constraints including heredoc source, static SVG output, and core Kino dependency."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "The diagram is readable, not over-dense, and uses consistent labels and styling."
    - "Text summary makes the visual structure understandable outside the SVG."
    - "Node and edge labels are clear and do not rely only on color."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles labels with spaces or special characters through quoting or sanitization."
    - "Avoids unsupported beta syntax unless a fallback is documented."
    - "Keeps generated source deterministic and bounded."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.Mermaid-centered and does not replace the diagram with a generic SVG library."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-mermaid
- canonical-widget

